Z||000003||Raydar||06-07-2001||09:56 AM||||Okay. Sixteen subs, eight mids and four tweeters? Is anything wrong with this picture? It'll make a whole hell of a lot of noise, rattle a bunch of windows and stuff, and maybe make some ears bleed, but is it useful for anything else? Is it even listenable? Wonder what the frequency response curve looks like.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I saw an article in a car stereo mag, a few years ago. They were talking about having blown the windshield out of a GMC pickup with pure SPL. Twice. The first time it just fell out onto the hood. The second time it shattered. <BR>Jeebus.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000004||JSocha||06-07-2001||10:08 AM||||On "Ripley's Believe It or Not" shown on TBS, they had a guy who has the loudest car stereo and had it in, I believe a Texas competition for loudest car stereo.<P>Anyways, he had shatter proof glass installed in the vehicle.  People's hair literally blows from the sound waves!  Kind of funny...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Back in 85/86 I could have bought a Mazda RX7 (which some guy rescued from a junkyard and rebuilt it custom on his own) with a custom home made oak dash, stereo and that had apparently been raced several times at the salt flats (somthing like 220+ MPH...per one of our vendors who knew the guy).  The guy that owned it (as told by the vendor who was visiting our family and watching my dad make old style German sausages) took it to a competion called (if I recall this right) "Decible High" and blew by shattering the windows out on the first note.  After that, the guy apparently installed lexan glass as the replacement of choice.<P>Didn't get the car; it was sold to some kid and a few months later it was totaled.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
